+# TODO 5 and 8: prepared experiment protocol
+
+Preparation date: 2026-11-10. Base: architect at e75941a17ecc4b6dbf51a3a6eefd1f4d82bfd221.
+This document records the user's choices and implementation decisions for review. Formal results have not been generated by preparation or timing probes.
+
+## Scope and choices
+
+- TODO 5: BPR, IKGR_kgoff, IKGR_dyn_nointent, each with seeds 2020, 2021, 2022 (9 fits).
+- TODO 8: MF-backbone IKGR_dyn with 0%, 5%, 10%, 20% intent removal and the same seeds (12 fits).
+- Reuse TODO 5's no-intent control for TODO 8. Do not generalize conclusions to LightGCN.
+- All 21 fits use one local RTX 2070 SUPER, the same dataset and protocol. No concurrent GPU fits.
+- Dedicated Python 3.11.18 environment, PyTorch 2.3.0+cu121 and RecBole 1.2.0. Keep the dependency freeze and environment evidence with the eventual PR.
+
+## Fixed protocol
+
+Use `configs/todo_5_8.yaml`: k=30, per-user temporal TO 80/10/10 split, train-only profiles and recency, 64 dimensions, train batch 2048, learning rate 0.001, regularization 0.000001, maximum 40 epochs, validation every 2 epochs and stopping patience 3. Select the checkpoint using validation NDCG@10. Keep existing deterministic, full-precision training.
+
+The user approved 128 users per full-sort evaluation batch. RecBole expresses its batch size as user-item score count; the launcher derives 128 * item_num (3,580,928 for 27,976 items including padding). Evaluate **all 62,142 validation users and all 62,142 test users**, against all items with the existing history masks. The 1,024-user timing sample is never a formal evaluation population.
+
+Earlier batch probes found matching rounded validation metrics but a few near-tie top-30 ordering differences. Batch changes are not bitwise-equivalent. Apply 128 consistently across all conditions and record the actual value in each result. Do not change precision, train batch, seed count, epoch cap or validation frequency to improve timing.
+
+## Intent filtering definition
+
+Count distinct items present in the train split connected to each intent, before the existing cap of 32. Only intents with positive train-item degree enter the percentage denominator. Sort by degree descending, then original intent ID ascending, and remove floor(active_count * percentage / 100). Remove every incident user and item edge. Preserve intent IDs, embedding rows and shape, and the order of remaining edges; then apply the existing cap and normalization. User-only or held-out-item-only intents are outside the removal denominator. Intent embeddings stay frozen as in IKGR_dyn.
+
+Save the complete removed-ID/degree list, counts and edge statistics separately for each condition/seed and reference its SHA256 prefix in the result. The real-data preflight found 114,794 positive-degree intents and removed 0 / 5,739 / 11,479 / 22,958. Removal sets must be nested. Zero removal is a no-op; empty filtered rows must remain finite.
+
+## Launch and validation
+
+From the repository directory, use the dedicated interpreter:
+
+```powershell
+. ..\Activate-Experiment.ps1
+..\venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts/run_todo_5_8.py --check
+..\venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q tests/
+```
+
+The check verifies full-data split sizes, train-only provenance, all selected models on CUDA, finite forward/backward values, full-sort predictions, and effective filter edges. It takes one training minibatch but performs no optimizer updates. Default behavior is check-only. Formal training requires the explicit command below, after the user instructs it to start:
+
+```powershell
+..\venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts/run_todo_5_8.py --run --phase all
+```
+
+`--phase 5` and `--phase 8` permit separate execution. The launcher clears inherited IKGR environment overrides and explicitly sets the approved seeds, metrics and reranking. CUDA is mandatory; CPU fallback fails. Outputs go to isolated `run_k30_TO/todo_5_8/`. Code/config/data/runtime fingerprints prevent reuse of stale results; a completed seed also requires requested per-user files and an intact filter-statistics artifact. JSON result updates use atomic replacement. Freeze the code/config before formal runs.
+
+## Requested pause and resume
+
+The user chose saving only when a pause is requested, to release the GPU for games without paying for a save every epoch. From a second terminal in the repository directory:
+
+```powershell
+..\venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts/run_todo_5_8.py --pause
+..\venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts/run_todo_5_8.py --status
+..\venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts/run_todo_5_8.py --resume --phase all
+```
+
+Use the same `--config` and `--phase` as the original launch. `--pause` requests a stop; it does not immediately kill the process. Wait for status `paused` and `gpu_released: true` before starting a GPU-heavy game. The child exits after finishing the current epoch and its scheduled validation, updating early stopping, and atomically saving the state. During preparation or final evaluation/export, stopping waits for that stage to finish. Between runs, completed results suffice and no training snapshot is needed.
+
+The snapshot includes current model/optimizer, Python/NumPy/CPU/CUDA random states, train/validation/test loader generators, completed epoch, early-stopping state, best validation metrics, loss history and accumulated active training time. It also embeds the best validation model independently of the latest model: a pause must not change model selection. Thus pause files are larger than ordinary best-only checkpoints. Snapshots are replaced atomically and are removed only after all per-user files and the completed result are committed. Pause duration and data reconstruction are excluded from `train_sec`.
+
+Resume rebuilds the identical dataset/model, rejects a changed code/data/config/seed fingerprint, restores state and continues at the next epoch. It does not rerun the seven-model preflight on every resume. A completed fit (including early stopping) resumes evaluation without another optimizer step. The implementation targets the fixed RecBole 1.2.0 protocol: one process, worker=0, uniform negatives and full precision. The OS lock prevents two launchers from using the same output directory. The parent launcher never retains a CUDA context; preflight runs in a separate child.
+
+This is controlled pause/resume, not automatic crash recovery. Force-killing during an epoch does not save that epoch; an unrequested crash may require restarting the current seed. Do not edit code/config, change hardware, or delete inputs while paused. A changed environment is refused rather than silently mixing experiments. The normal training checkpoint still follows the existing best-validation policy when no pause is requested.
+
+## Later analysis and PR contents
+
+Evaluate popularity penalties 0.25, 0.5, 1.0 without extra model fits. Retain validation and test per-user outputs for every variant. Choose the representative removal rate by mean validation NDCG@10 over three seeds; break ties toward the smaller rate. Publish every rate's results, seed means/standard deviations, paired user bootstrap intervals and Wilcoxon comparisons. Test results must not choose the representative condition.
+
+Include this decision record, code, exact commands, package freeze, checks, data/code hashes, raw metrics, filter artifacts, paired analysis and limitations in the PR targeting architect through a user-owned fork. Do not mix temporary timing metrics or obsolete 512-dimensional results into accuracy claims. No PR is created or merged during environment preparation.
